A non-mayor session that Mike directs is a WORKER, not the mayor. Mike corrected this twice on 2026-09-26: "you are NOT the mayor", then "you are to open PRs and babysit them to green".

What it does, at his direction:
- create the worktree;
- push the branch;
- open the PR, as a draft until every step has landed;
- babysit CI to green;
- mark the PR ready.
It may use background subagents for the steps, and it may file beads for defects it finds.

What stays with the mayor session:
- merging, on its criterion;
- the dispatch ledger ai/worktree-agent-ids.tsv, where the worker adds no rows;
- the tracker checkpoint and commits on main.
Tell the mayor when a PR is ready, and before any shadow-cljs run, because the build lane is machine-wide.
